<title>USA: U.S. aluminum output up 200,000 tonnes in 1996.</title>
<headline>U.S. aluminum output up 200,000 tonnes in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. primary aluminum production rose more than 200,000 tonnes to 3,576,726 tonnes in 1996 compared to the previous year's total of 3,375,241 tonnes, the Aluminum Association reported.</p>
<p>The average daily rate of production in December fell slightly to 9,827 tonnes compared to 9,832 tonnes in November.</p>
<p>Actual production in December was 304,644 tonnes compared to 294,954 tonnes in November, the association said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
